  "notes": "Transcribed from the official Loma Linda University 2026-2027 Catalog (effective Summer Quarter 2026) program page 'Physical Therapy - D.P.T. (Entry Level)' (School of Allied Health Professions, Department of Physical Therapy). The catalog publishes the three-year curriculum split by First, Second, and Third Year; year sums verified: First Year: 69, Second Year: 65.5, Third Year: 19 = 153.5 = catalog Total Units 153.5. PHTH 505 (Acute Care Simulation) is listed at 1 unit in the First Year and 0.5 units in the Second Year exactly as the catalog lists it; allow_repeated_courses is set because the published year tables are transcribed verbatim. PHTH 723: the catalog curriculum table lists the code with blank title and units in the Third Year; the catalog's Total Units 153.5 reconciles with this row contributing 0 units, so it is encoded as a required 0-credit slot (excluded from sums) with the blank row documented rather than omitted. The catalog's service-learning footnote appears on the curriculum table; the specific course it annotates is not recoverable from the published table, so it is documented here without being assigned to a course. Clinical experiences: integrated experiences in years 1-2 plus terminal clinical experiences PHTH 711 and 712 (7 units each) in the third year. Normal time to complete: 3 years (12 academic quarters), full-time enrollment. Entrance requires an earned bachelor's degree in any field plus the listed prerequisite courses (anatomy and physiology, chemistry, physics sequences with labs; biological sciences; statistics; medical terminology; psychology; human growth and development; speech) and 80 hours observation; documented here and not placed in any term. Per-course prerequisites are not published in the curriculum tables; the published year order is the official sequence, so prereq arrays are intentionally empty.",
